        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-20363",
        ":question/problem": "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$, $y$, and $z,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is \n\n$$\\begin{cases}0x+2y+3z=0 \\\\ 2x+0y+3z=2 \\\\ 2x+3y+0z=3.\\end{cases}$$\n\nBy simplifying, we obtain: \n\n$$\\begin{cases}2y+3z=0 \\\\ 2x+3z=2 \\\\ 2x+3y=3\\end{cases}$$"
      },
